      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does STS provide electronics recycling in Billings, Montana?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS Electronic Recycling provides electronics recycling services for Billings, Montana organizations, including businesses, healthcare providers, schools, public agencies, and industrial operations. Billings projects can include computers, laptops, servers, monitors, printers, networking equipment, and mobile devices. Pickup options depend on project scope, equipment volume, access requirements, and scheduling availability. STS also supports secure data destruction and documentation for Billings organizations that need a structured process for retiring workplace technology."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does data destruction support Billings electronics recycling projects?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Billings organizations can select secure data destruction certified data destruction for hard drives and other digital media before electronics are processed for recycling. STS uses documented chain-of-custody procedures and can provide destruction documentation based on the project scope. The approach helps Billings healthcare, energy, education, government, and commercial teams manage devices that may contain sensitive information. NIST SP 800-88 guidance can inform decisions about media sanitization and physical destruction methods."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is electronics recycling pickup available in the Billings area?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS coordinates scheduled electronics recycling pickup for qualifying Billings projects. Organizations can provide their equipment list, estimated volume, building access information, and desired collection date to discuss logistics. Complimentary pickup may be available for qualifying volumes. Billings organizations with multiple sites or large technology refreshes can also discuss consolidated collection planning. Service availability depends on the specific project, equipment type, timing, and logistics requirements."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications does STS use for Billings electronics recycling?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS Electronic Recycling provides certified processing for electronics recycling and secure data destruction certified data destruction for hard drives and digital media. certified processing applies to secure recycling and downstream processing practices. secure data destruction applies to secure destruction services rather than electronics recycling itself. Billings organizations can use these service options to support documented retirement of computers, servers, network equipment, storage media, and other electronic assets."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How quickly can a Billings electronics recycling project be scheduled?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Scheduling for Billings electronics recycling depends on project size, equipment type, pickup access, and fleet availability. Organizations seeking a Billings pickup should contact STS with an equipment inventory and preferred timeframe. Same-week scheduling may be available for some projects, but timing is not guaranteed. Advance planning can help accommodate office moves, technology refreshes, lease returns, departmental cleanouts, and projects requiring documentation or secure hard drive destruction."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can Billings healthcare and public-sector organizations use STS services?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS supports Billings healthcare organizations, public agencies, education teams, and commercial operations with electronics recycling and secure data destruction planning. Billings Clinic, St. Vincent Healthcare, schools, municipal teams, and similar organizations may need documented handling for retired technology. STS can coordinate chain-of-custody records, hard drive destruction, asset reporting, and certified processing recycling based on the equipment and documentation requirements of each Billings project."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens after electronics are picked up from a Billings organization?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "After collection from a Billings organization, equipment is evaluated for reuse, asset remarketing, material recovery, data destruction, or certified processing electronics recycling. The selected path depends on device condition, business requirements, and whether storage media requires secure destruction. STS maintains a documented workflow for electronics disposition. Billings customers can request documentation appropriate to their project, including chain-of-custody records, asset details, or certificates of destruction for selected media destruction services."
          }
        },
